        "math_academy_id": "q-105411",
        "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,q(t)=7t-3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)\u22a5{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $2{t}^{2}+2t.$",
        "worked_solution": "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=2{t}^{2}+2t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{\u27e8q(t),{p}_{2}(t)\u27e9}{\u27e8{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\u27e9}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8q(t),{p}_{2}(t)\u27e9 & =q(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(7t\\,-\\,3){|}_{-1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,-\\,t){|}_{-1}+(7t\\,-\\,3){|}_{0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,-\\,t){|}_{0}+(7t\\,-\\,3){|}_{1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,-\\,t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-20,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\u27e9 & ={p}_{2}(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+{p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)^{2}{|}_{-1}+({t}^{2}-t)^{2}{|}_{0}+({t}^{2}-t)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{-20}{4}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-t)=-5{t}^{2}+5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}+2t+(-5{t}^{2}+5t) \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}+7t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
